    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (48 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-duplicate detection for owner creation. When a new owner passes the hard-duplicate (identity key) check but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while carrying a *different* telephone, it is still created and flagged as a possible duplicate.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After the existing hard-duplicate (identity key \u2192 409) check, added a soft-duplicate scan: it finds existing owners with a matching last name (case-insensitive, via the existing `householdKey` normalization), the same postcode, and a different telephone. If any match, it sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the lowest matching owner id (deterministic); otherwise `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 Added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean, coalesced to non-null `false` in the getter, mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer, null when not a possible duplicate) fields with getters/setters.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` as read-only properties on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes them and MapStruct maps them by name.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 Added the `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns. The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema addition is what makes the columns exist under test.\n\nThe new `Cp35Tests.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` passes, and all 48 existing + new tests remain green.",
